#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124142 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f232aed9-1584-5e57-a881-226a6876384a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/id #uuid "001af492-25b1-5f75-b030-668708eee118" :question/math-academy-id "e-15602" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/assets/a664a3af1ba466491d209dadd32a3be026a5179ac2d0281b55f30917f9ab016b.png)\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+2t \\\\ 5t \\\\ 1-t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 5t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124143 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/id #uuid "7a6038c2-3f7b-5dfa-a9e2-256b246fcc20" :question/math-academy-id "e-15603" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/assets/f161e07945eb3fe2350a56ab5cb96fa0ae2d055eb3b4cc633abfae30839ec76f.png)\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5-t \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-t \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(5,3,1)$ and is parallel to the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/assets/11701a2d63851a3f241d8bd905693abaaa6eda6fe4ba0c5710c92d8189595ffd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124144 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/id #uuid "173b99e8-d00c-57c8-995e-ba198361480e" :question/math-academy-id "e-15604" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/assets/53386f04f4025fda6ab579113a8ecb53a19f4dc0a77903adc05bac3a71429717.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(3,3,-5)$ and $Q(1,0,-1)$. Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ -3t \\\\ 4t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3-2t \\\\ 3-3t \\\\ -5+4t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-2t \\\\ y=3-3t \\\\ z=-5+4t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124145 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/id #uuid "a9c13555-9d30-5dfc-be5a-13f0597c2ada" :question/math-academy-id "e-15605" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overline{PQ},$ where $P(1,-5,3)$ and $Q(0, 4, -4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-t \\\\ 9t \\\\ -7t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-t \\\\ -5+9t \\\\ 3-7t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t \\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$ are the following:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/assets/c3747cbb9a88a419d6808959c490089c79041cc8773651fac1953f4846839c14.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f232aed9-1584-5e57-a881-226a6876384a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd323aed-3450-563b-97e6-1afb42a770a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387754} {:answer/id #uuid "f9aca740-deb3-5d5f-810c-5296551e03a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387755} {:answer/id #uuid "aec5f9c1-809f-56c6-8761-17b4ee813b07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387756} {:answer/id #uuid "ab359ccf-5f90-51ce-bf5e-58cb4e6d3b6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387757} {:answer/id #uuid "aa54d7b8-eba9-560c-91de-b1e84cddda06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa54d7b8-eba9-560c-91de-b1e84cddda06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387758} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bfd9f64-59f8-5d07-a1fe-ccb0bfeb4cb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6c0a26c-6007-59ae-8900-248c9a828cd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-126997" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-3 \\\\ y=5t \\\\ z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5t \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f232aed9-1584-5e57-a881-226a6876384a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba5cb508-5b9e-5629-a19d-3f649a491961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387761} {:answer/id #uuid "2ba8fa2c-823c-5a8d-9a70-658f561138b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387762} {:answer/id #uuid "c07daa07-c826-5c7f-94b4-f740c06bfb80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387763} {:answer/id #uuid "28be3cea-2129-59a7-96ed-0eb016b1f676" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387764} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec212a5-0ea4-59ce-99a2-2fe178606855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba5cb508-5b9e-5629-a19d-3f649a491961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387761} :answer-field/id #uuid "1757839a-1708-50ac-a382-316bfc887f23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36cc5d87-ef5c-5ced-b253-0194de848513" :question/math-academy-id "q-127002" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=13-8t \\\\ y=7t \\\\ z=-7-3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13-8t \\\\ 7t \\\\ -7-3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-8t \\\\ 7t \\\\ -3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d313486-e349-59a2-b8d5-02e13fbf6d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314761} {:answer/id #uuid "6eab4365-8239-52a0-a5f3-dd30891fced6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314762} {:answer/id #uuid "e97f4fd1-8bdf-5b77-8a43-223fd5730ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314763} {:answer/id #uuid "1e232130-0aa4-523d-ad8b-da996a44179d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314764} {:answer/id #uuid "a27c9435-0f0a-5c61-a3d5-13481412c664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d313486-e349-59a2-b8d5-02e13fbf6d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314761} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8e2521f-de41-5643-ba87-56daab4b42c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11bd8602-a2be-5ae4-8ba8-6a2ffe62757c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127043" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ y=5-4t \\\\ z=2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector parallel to the line that points in the direction of increasing $t$." :question/worked-solution "Write the position vector as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\begin{pmatrix}-2\\\\5\\\\\\frac17\\end{pmatrix}\n+t\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac13\\\\-4\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFor any positive increment $h$,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t+h)-\\mathbf r(t)=h\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac13\\\\-4\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\left(\\frac13,-4,2\\right)$ is parallel to the line and points in the direction of increasing $t$. Its negative $\\left(-\\frac13,4,-2\\right)$ is also parallel, but points in the direction of decreasing $t$ and does not satisfy the requested orientation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe4f0806-0fc7-5f51-ab81-33fd4d32ccfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-4+3t \\\\ y=-3-2t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387768} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ddd0e3-169d-5e9b-8f17-a7d714cb10d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=-5+2t \\\\ z=-4+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387769} {:answer/id #uuid "bb231cec-4e63-5ff7-8207-763b171ae0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2+t \\\\ y=-5+3t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387770} {:answer/id #uuid "e87a1dd0-1e22-5b27-9312-97289bb0037b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=5-2t \\\\ z=-4-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387771} {:answer/id #uuid "aad1915d-54db-591d-a400-e033fe1da95d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4-2t \\\\ y=-5-2t \\\\ z=2+3t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb231cec-4e63-5ff7-8207-763b171ae0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2+t \\\\ y=-5+3t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387770} :answer-field/id #uuid "a66bd7bc-2429-563d-bbe0-27f9dd15047b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "453b8dde-1343-580a-bb17-743f24caa02f" :question/math-academy-id "q-127046" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(2,-5,4)$ and $Q(3,-2,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 3t \\\\ -2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+t \\\\ -5+3t \\\\ 4-2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2+t \\\\ y=-5+3t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87c2d36b-627d-5f64-8a6c-a09f1ad9c528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314789} {:answer/id #uuid "6753ca76-c745-5e12-977d-db60884dea68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3-7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314790} {:answer/id #uuid "b42ef42e-1337-5b35-ba54-883e7d684a97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11-2t \\\\ z=4+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314791} {:answer/id #uuid "00448bb0-44e2-58c8-92b1-aeda5e4b0a22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=11+2t \\\\ z=3-7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314792} {:answer/id #uuid "d5bdabce-6dcf-5334-a2f9-c1909f66c74a" :answer/