\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b80a7c1-1043-53df-9937-1c302aea271a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357326} {:answer/id #uuid "c7131830-fa04-52c9-8165-83976213e7df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4+t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=2-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357327} {:answer/id #uuid "26149efd-6258-5c6d-899b-8b76bd92f6a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357328} {:answer/id #uuid "a1bd0392-0d4d-5e20-af94-0f8eea17c8ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=5+t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357329} {:answer/id #uuid "31cb1ef6-a234-5bb7-b23d-06c409656e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=-t \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b80a7c1-1043-53df-9937-1c302aea271a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357326} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9a7ef8f-c4b6-5c5b-9714-eade580df09e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3a37d06-4a0c-5126-bd3b-fbb999a13c7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-36026" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1+4t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af13daa6-8282-50d0-96db-5f6997cac18a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387822} {:answer/id #uuid "af858222-d63f-5d13-a3a3-1b9b5c0ec7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387823} {:answer/id #uuid "192132d9-79fb-549d-8347-4aa0e57fa7cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387824} {:answer/id #uuid "285755ae-67db-51a3-b559-4cadb6e6e2c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387825} {:answer/id #uuid "4fe72ae3-39a9-5cc2-86b7-f79794ad112d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af858222-d63f-5d13-a3a3-1b9b5c0ec7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387823} :answer-field/id #uuid "51759681-959a-5123-88be-afd698623649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1a4efcc-8584-528a-9f17-a5e1e08f2760" :question/math-academy-id "q-70716" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2t+1 \\\\ y=3-t \\\\ z=t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2t+1 \\\\ 3-t \\\\ t+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ -t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(1,3,2)$  and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78eef5db-136a-55b0-811f-d71f51241e67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387829} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a773c6-5be2-56e8-bb56-4ecc7d8d3bda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387830} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd3e558-ef7c-526c-90d4-9450a49dc721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387831} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb39529-c07c-5d59-90a9-073c581c1607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387832} {:answer/id #uuid "3d7290ec-e202-515c-a116-00f84a3b36b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdd3e558-ef7c-526c-90d4-9450a49dc721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387831} :answer-field/id #uuid "58a9fdb3-e40a-5d2e-86c5-c2dac7c00c95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b35cb98-4ef1-509b-b779-5ff2e485c987" :question/math-academy-id "q-70721" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=t-1 \\\\ y=-t+1 \\\\ z=-t-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}t-1 \\\\ -t+1 \\\\ -t-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ -t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-1,1,-1)$   and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
